        "original_id": "d0b8466f-b927-500a-98c5-80ceb13df0f0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Manfred Moch, Bert Kaempfert\n- Roles: solo trumpet player, orchestra leader, music producer, songwriter\n- Organizations: Bert Kaempfert orchestra\n- Topics: 1960s popular music, hit songs\n\nFacts:\n- Bert Kaempfert, born Berthold Heinrich Kämpfert, was a German orchestra leader, music producer, and songwriter.\n- Bert Kaempfert was born on 16 October 1923 and died on 21 June 1980.\n- In the 1960s, Manfred Moch became known as the featured solo trumpet player for the Bert Kaempfert orchestra.\n- Manfred Moch contributed memorable and melodic trumpet solos to many of Bert Kaempfert’s hits.\n- Songs associated with Manfred Moch’s featured solos for Bert Kaempfert included “Bye Bye Blues,” “Strangers In The Night,” “L-O-V-E,” and “Sweet Maria.”",
